      "content": "According to the Arrhenius equation,",
      "options": [
        {
          "identifier": "A",
          "content": "a high activation energy usually implies a fast reaction"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "B",
          "content": "rate constant increases with increase in temperature. This is due to a greater number of collisions whose energy exceeds the activation energy"
        },
        {
          "identifier": "C",
          "content": "higher the magnitude of activation energy, stronger is the temperature dependence of the rate constant."
        },
        {
          "identifier": "D",
          "content": "the pre-exponential factor is a measure of the rate at which collisions occur, irrespective of their\nenergy."
        }
      ],
      "correct_options": [
        "B",
        "C",
        "D"
      ],
      "explanation": "The Arrhenius equation is a mathematical model of the temperature dependence of reaction rates. It is expressed as follows:\n\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.025ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"13.283ex\" height=\"2.227ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -973.4 5870.9 984.4\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(798.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msup\" transform=\"translate(1854.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use><use data-c=\"65\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-65\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(1227,443.1) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mo\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(778,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"45\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-45\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(714,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1916.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"2F\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2F\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2416.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"52\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-52\"></use><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\" transform=\"translate(736,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n\n<br><br>where :\n<br><br>- k is the rate constant\n<br><br>- A is the pre-exponential factor (also known as the frequency factor)\n<br><br>- E<sub>a</sub> is the activation energy\n<br><br>- R is the universal gas constant\n<br><br>- T is the temperature (in Kelvin)\n<br><br>- e is Euler's number, a mathematical constant approximately equal to 2.71828\n\n<br><br>The options provided correlate to the Arrhenius equation as follows:\n\n<br><br>Option A : Incorrect. A high activation energy usually implies a slower reaction, not a fast one. The activation energy is the energy barrier that needs to be overcome for a reaction to occur. The higher the activation energy, the fewer the number of molecules that have enough energy to surpass this barrier and react, resulting in a slower reaction rate.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Chemical Kinetics and Nuclear Chemistry Question 49 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1li7eo95u/8e1ef974-f342-4a45-89a8-56066f4c5be1/61a11420-fd54-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7eo95v.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<br>Option B : Correct. Temperature <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.621ex\" height=\"1.871ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 1158.6 827\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> is greater than <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.621ex\" height=\"1.871ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -677 1158.6 827\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"54\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-54\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(755,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"31\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-31\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>; hence, the fraction of molecules (shaded in green) having energy greater than activation energy increases with increase in temperature result, rate of reaction increases.\n<br><br>Higher temperature, more number of collisions (between extents) having energy greater than activation energy happen increases speed of reaction.\n<br><br><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2016 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Chemical Kinetics and Nuclear Chemistry Question 49 English Explanation 2\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1li7f4hyi/83c9d7e4-5343-49c2-8f7e-a19d9176fd14/255ed4a0-fd56-11ed-9057-a7f9a0e389da/file-1li7f4hyj.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n<br><br>Option C : Correct. A reaction at higher activation energy makes the reaction rate slow. An increase in temperature causes reactant molecules to cross the high energy barrier; i.e., <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.355ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.704ex\" height=\"1.894ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -680 1195.1 837.1\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(771,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> and form activated complex.\n\n<br><br>Option D : Correct. The pre-exponential factor (A) takes into account the probability of proper orientation of reactant molecules to form the product and the frequency at which reactant molecules collide to form the product.\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.345ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"12.923ex\" height=\"1.965ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -716 5712 868.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1027.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"3D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-3D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(2083.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"5A\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-5A\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(644,-152.7) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"41\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-41\"></use><use data-c=\"42\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-42\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"></use></g></g></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4030.7,0)\"><use data-c=\"D7\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-D7\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(5031,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"50\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-50\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>\n<br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.345ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"4.147ex\" height=\"1.891ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -683 1833 835.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D44D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" transform=\"translate(716,-152.7) scale(0.707)\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D434\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D434\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(750,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D435\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D435\"></use></g></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> : Collision frequency or frequency with which A collides with B.\n<br><br>P : Probability of reactant molecules oriented in right orientation with respect to each other to form the product.\n<br><br>Option (D), where pre-exponential factor affects the rate reaction irrespective of the energy they possess."
